<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="8.3A" level="1">Commercial Code — Negotiable Instruments</unit>
		<unit label="part" identifier="1" level="2">General Provisions and Definitions</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>8.3A-114</section_number>
	<catch_line>Contradictory terms of instrument</catch_line>
	<text>
		If an instrument contains contradictory terms, typewritten terms prevail over printed terms, handwritten terms prevail over both, and words prevail over numbers.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, §§ 6-369, 6-420; 1964, c. 219, § 8.3-118; 1992, c. 693.</history>
</law>
